## pyfia

This product includes software derived from **pyfia** by Mihiar & Mohler,
originally licensed under the MIT License ("MIT").

Modifications: The original pyfia is a Python toolkit for USDA Forest
Inventory & Analysis (FIA) data. Anamata Kāhui forked it to extract the
biomass → carbon estimation math (under Apache-2.0), strip US-specific
data loaders (FIA EVALIDator, USFS APIs), and add:

  1. A te reo Māori internationalisation layer for CLI messages
  2. An iwi/hapū attestation overlay on top of every estimate
  3. JSON-Schema definitions for the attestation document
  4. New Zealand–context biomass expansion factors (Douglas-fir,
     radiata pine, native podocarps where data permits)

